{"lines":[{"w":0.070273335774739598,"t":"Reading","h":0.015994695953091442,"c":1,"x":0.84550636663340339,"y":0.058591650196965328},{"w":0.71635787963867192,"y":0.10317491421249048,"t":"Nevertheless, in many cases REM sleep does seem to have benefits. Growing evidence","h":0.020568896374392187,"x":0.19544722537528325,"c":1},{"x":0.19377163613860149,"t":"from birds and mammals suggests that REM sleep and dreaming are important for","h":0.018914674528000552,"y":0.12209302328400018,"w":0.6799307759602865,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.1394889053371059,"h":0.021902054986226216,"w":0.72336349487304685,"t":"forming memories and learning. It is believed that when events are replayed in dreams,","x":0.19196061333554459},{"w":0.7129605611165365,"c":1,"h":0.021583619194484482,"x":0.19195553794984485,"y":0.15823454774543366,"t":"this helps to integrate memories into longer-term storage. As soon as animals evolved"},{"t":"moderately complex lifestyles, they would have needed to dream in order to manage","h":0.021257089517431882,"c":1,"x":0.19370150623580323,"y":0.17663025609388483,"w":0.70429499308268229},{"x":0.19204152476059572,"t":"these litestyles.","w":0.13148788452148436,"h":0.015988371937820545,"y":0.19622093029683585,"c":1},{"y":0.23105907224184297,"x":0.19367384976214141,"c":1,"t":"However, we still don't understand how this outward behaviour relates to internal","w":0.67145960489908862,"h":0.021581404854819186},{"x":0.19368468890098522,"c":1,"h":0.0218672822454411,"w":0.6714523824055989,"t":"experience. It seems impossible to know what it is like to be a rat or a pigeon, let","y":0.24864467975243798},{"c":1,"x":0.19198950570302439,"w":0.68869130452473959,"t":"alone imagine their dreamscapes. We are quick to interpret the twitching limbs and","h":0.02090736533312465,"y":0.26716013342240652},{"c":1,"x":0.19377162020426036,"y":0.28779069739219443,"w":0.70588236490885414,"t":"quiet barks of sleeping dogs, but the truth is that we don't know if there is an internal","h":0.01744186102384615},{"w":0.47577855428059895,"h":0.019019439222096923,"y":0.30510846771443423,"c":1,"t":"experience of chasing rabbits that comes along with that.","x":0.1920415185218432},{"c":1,"t":"Another non-human dreamer offers insight here. In 2019, while making a documentary,","x":0.19189468650517769,"w":0.72005030314127605,"h":0.024191437942152505,"y":0.33891487001528509},{"w":0.69723180135091134,"x":0.19377164415585915,"t":"David Scheel of Alaska Pacific University in the USA housed an octopus named Heidi","y":0.35899230261632498,"h":0.018914673860628617,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.021471486715606392,"w":0.69912567138671877,"x":0.19022469380639032,"y":0.37747995954220115,"t":"in a tank in his living room. At one point, in the middle of the night, Heidi seemed to"},{"y":0.39645628922823328,"x":0.19198146471657254,"w":0.71118733723958338,"t":"dream: her limbs and head moved, and her skin rapidly changed colour, as though she","h":0.021031667336957049,"c":1},{"y":0.41567529714428375,"t":"was pursuing a crab.","c":1,"w":0.17301038106282554,"h":0.017494751574527734,"x":0.19204152226054225},{"y":0.45032899307097052,"c":1,"x":0.19193397962506481,"t":"Similarly, a report recently emerged of a sleeping octopus apparently having a","w":0.64725941975911461,"h":0.021710369785487682},{"x":0.19195934246811741,"t":"nightmare. Costello, as the octopus was called, thrashed around, extended his mantle","y":0.4693322299419378,"w":0.70777277628580726,"h":0.02132482108242284,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.19195216837341045,"h":0.022845562560479982,"y":0.48740324009403535,"t":"as if trying to make himself look bigger, and squirted ink as though he were being","w":0.67318567911783844},{"y":0.50726744188721129,"h":0.018974685268522196,"w":0.66782007853190095,"t":"attacked by a predator. The nightmare study is intriguing, says Scheel, but is only","x":0.19204151769457176,"c":1},{"y":0.52469053269952948,"t":"based on one animal. He argues that as well as outward behaviour, brain imaging is","c":1,"h":0.020679317044577705,"x":0.19198696069754836,"w":0.68522491455078127},{"c":1,"y":0.54345687533166076,"h":0.019847828495994646,"t":"needed to show that the octopuses are replaying sequences of activities from their","x":0.19199534967238491,"w":0.68347625732421879},{"c":1,"x":0.19031141705537066,"y":0.56249999970721831,"t":"waking lives in dreams.","h":0.01744186102384615,"w":0.19377162933349609},{"x":0.19021243642486296,"y":0.59708458548775623,"h":0.020844513590808078,"t":"The trouble is that we will never be able to experience any animal's dreams. That goes","w":0.71127136230468746,"c":1},{"w":0.70615758260091144,"c":1,"y":0.61527107123010094,"h":0.022223897711057816,"t":"for other humans' dreams too. But we can try to imagine what these dreamscapes are","x":0.19015353122916034},{"t":"like by meeting animals on their own terms. For example, vision is the dominant sense","x":0.19018888362117442,"h":0.02298295306024889,"w":0.70956654866536462,"y":0.63382096748131789,"c":1},{"t":"for many humans, and so our dreams are heavily visual too. Dogs primarily navigate the","c":1,"w":0.7216296386718748,"y":0.6525731781808829,"h":0.021348843798093542,"x":0.18849046401136443},{"h":0.021672912207911121,"t":"world using smell while spiders rely much more on vibrations.","x":0.19021074497088419,"y":0.67041894996739226,"w":0.50719207763671881,"c":1},{"w":0.69908930460611973,"x":0.19024591101550545,"h":0.020138790592436506,"y":0.70763893151310597,"t":"It is likely that dreaming has served multiple purposes since the first complex animals","c":1},{"y":0.72635312858070178,"w":0.65235850016276042,"x":0.19025174246648816,"t":"evolved. And if this is the case, it is possible that better understanding of these","c":1,"h":0.020517812399200142},{"x":0.19031141216140687,"y":0.74562631196186746,"h":0.017494751574527623,"t":"purposes might shed light on the true purpose of our own dreams.","w":0.55190312703450517,"c":1},{"w":0.025951557159423877,"x":0.88581314866942307,"y":0.9563953488533169,"h":0.015988371937820545,"t":"39","c":1}],"h":2857,"w":2400}